.\" linotron202.ms — the figures of Condon, Kernighan and Thompson,
.\" "Experience with the Mergenthaler Linotron 202 Phototypesetter, or,
.\" How We Spent Our Summer Vacation" (Bell Laboratories, 1980), set
.\" again: pic for the drawings, chess for the board.  Made by make.sh
.\" from the sources beside it; the original, scanned, and its 2013
.\" reconstruction are at www.cs.princeton.edu/~bwk/202/.
.\"
.\"	book -m memo linotron202.ms		# linotron202.pdf
.p
.\" the memo's typewriter labels are bold
.bd CR 36
.alt "A block diagram: a disk of character definitions feeding a CPU, a 16-bit minicomputer, which also takes input and drives a CRT that exposes paper drawn past rollers."
.PS
D: circle rad 0.33 "DISK" "(character" "defns)"
arrow right 0.75 from D.e
C: box wid 1.0 ht 0.65 "CPU" "(16-bit mini)"
arrow from C.n + (0, 0.75) to C.n
"input" rjust at C.n + (-0.08, 0.68)
arrow right 0.65 from C.e
T: box wid 0.68 ht 0.2
"CRT" ljust at T.w + (0.06, 0)
line from T.ne to T.ne + (0.12, 0) to T.ne + (0.72, 0.33) to T.se + (0.72, -0.33) to T.se + (0.12, 0) to T.se
P: T.e + (0.92, 0)
arrow from P + (0, 1.3) to P + (0, -0.75)
circle rad 0.06 at P + (-0.065, 0.95)
circle rad 0.06 at P + (0.065, 0.95)
"rollers" ljust at P + (0.22, 0.97)
arrow from P + (0.75, -0.42) to P + (0.07, -0.42)
"paper" ljust at P + (0.78, -0.42)
.PE
.ce
Figure 1:  Basic Digital Typesetter
.bp
.alt "The outline of a letter e as chains of short vectors, each running left to right; Create marks where a pair of chains begins, Destroy where it ends."
.PS
